lator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids, January to February and August to September each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those years. In 2025 on that middle, February to March got 38% of normal and August to September got 44%, while 2026 so far shows April to May at 139%. Every grid&rsquo;s driest year was 1988.</p>"}
